# width is copied into measure behind its guard. What the copy gives is an integer and what the slow version gives is a number, and `wide & 16` leans on that:
# each of the two walks what is left of the block for itself, inside the walk of the call. Each binds the call by hand, so each stores behind its own binding.
# The closure behind the branches has two stores in front of it and none that stands in front of both ways: the verifier asks by ways.
